Part 2  
IBM Platform Vulnerabilities

Executive Vulnerability Summary

-  CVE-2026-9006. IBM WebSphere Application Server is affected by a server-side request forgery vulnerability when Ajax Proxy is configured, which can allow unauthorized requests from the system and lead to security bypass or information disclosure. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/node/7276600)

○ Mechanism. An attacker can send crafted requests through the Ajax Proxy, and if target validation is weak, the proxy may forward those requests using the server’s network identity. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/node/7276600)

○ Impact. The flaw can expose internal services or metadata endpoints and may be used to bypass network controls. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/node/7276600)

-  CVE-2026-11714. IBM WebSphere Application Server Liberty is affected by a server-side request forgery vulnerability in the apiDiscovery-1.0 component. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/ph71556ibm-websphere-application-server-affected-server-side-request-forgery-cve-2026-9006)

