-  CVE-2026-11546. IBM WebSphere Application Server Liberty is affected by a server-side request forgery vulnerability in the adminCenter-1.0 component. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/ph71556ibm-websphere-application-server-affected-server-side-request-forgery-cve-2026-9006)

○ Mechanism. An authenticated attacker with low-level privileges can use the administrative interface to bypass system boundaries and issue requests to internal systems. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/ph71556ibm-websphere-application-server-affected-server-side-request-forgery-cve-2026-9006)

○ Impact. The flaw can enable internal pivoting and unauthorized access to backend resources. [ibm](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/ph71556ibm-websphere-application-server-affected-server-side-request-forgery-cve-2026-9006)

-  CVE-2026-8633. IBM Web Server Plug-ins for WebSphere Application Server and WebSphere Liberty are vulnerable to remote code execution through a specially crafted request. [nvd.nist](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8633)

○ Mechanism. A specially crafted HTTP request can trigger code injection in the plug-in component that bridges front-end web servers and backend application servers. [cyberveille.esante.gouv](https://cyberveille.esante.gouv.fr/alertes/ibm-cve-2026-8633-2026-05-27)

○ Impact. Successful exploitation can lead to arbitrary code execution on the affected system with the privileges of the web server process. [nvd.nist](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8633)

